# Sprint 2 – Project Planning & Requirement Analysis

## Project Name
Inventory Management System

## Project Domain
Business

## Project Description
The Inventory Management System is a web-based application developed using the MERN Stack to help businesses manage products, categories, suppliers, inventory and purchase orders efficiently.

## Sprint 2 Objective
To analyze project requirements, identify stakeholders, define project scope, and document functional and non-functional requirements.

## Problem Statement
Manual inventory management can lead to inaccurate stock records, difficulty tracking products, supplier management problems and purchasing errors. A centralized system is required to improve inventory operations.

## Project Objectives
- Manage products and categories.
- Maintain supplier information.
- Monitor stock availability.
- Record stock transactions.
- Manage purchase orders.
- Generate inventory reports.

## Stakeholders
1. Administrator
2. Inventory Manager
3. Staff

## Project Scope
### Included
- User Authentication
- Product Management
- Category Management
- Supplier Management
- Inventory Management
- Purchase Order Management
- Inventory Reports

### Excluded
- Mobile Application
- AI-based Forecasting
- Payment Gateway
- Third-party Integrations

## Functional Requirements
- User Registration and Login
- Product CRUD Operations
- Category Management
- Supplier Management
- Stock In and Stock Out
- Stock Adjustment
- Inventory History
- Purchase Order Management
- Order Status Tracking
- Report Generation

## Non-Functional Requirements
- Performance
- Security
- Usability
- Reliability
- Maintainability
- Scalability

## Technology Stack
- Frontend: React.js
- Backend: Node.js and Express.js
- Database: MongoDB
- Authentication: JWT

## Sprint 2 Deliverables
- Problem Statement
- Project Objectives
- Stakeholder Identification
- Project Scope
- Functional Requirements
- Non-Functional Requirements
- Project Documentation

## Result
Project planning and requirement analysis were completed successfully. The requirements were identified and documented, providing a foundation for the next development sprint.
